-    as written.
+    Slash dates are always day first (``03/04/2026`` is 3 April 2026); day
+    and month take one or two digits, the year exactly four. Surrounding
+    whitespace is ignored. A slash date with a two-digit year raises
+    ValueError saying it is ambiguous; anything else that does not parse,
+    including a day that does not exist, raises ValueError saying it is an
+    invalid date. Both messages name the text as written.
     """
